# Split service

A small HTTP JSON service for groups of people who share expenses: who paid what, who owes whom. Node.js 24.2 or later, no dependencies.

## Run

```
npm start
```

| Env | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `PORT` | `3000` | Port to listen on (127.0.0.1 only) |
| `DATA_FILE` | `groups.json` | Where the store is kept |

On start it prints `listening on http://127.0.0.1:<port>`. A missing data file is an empty store. Every change is written to the data file atomically (temp file, then rename), so a crash never leaves half a file.

## Test

```
npm test
```

## API

| Route | Body | Success | Errors |
|---|---|---|---|
| `POST /groups` | `{id, name, members}` | 201 the group | 400 invalid, 409 `group already exists` |
| `GET /groups/:id` | | 200 `{id, name, members}` | 404 |
| `POST /groups/:id/expenses` | `{description, payer, amount, split?}` | 201 the expense | 400 invalid, 404 unknown group |
| `GET /groups/:id/expenses` | | 200 `{expenses}`, sorted by id | 404 |
| `PATCH /groups/:id/expenses/:expenseId` | any of `{description, payer, amount, split}` | 200 the changed expense | 400 invalid, 404 |
| `DELETE /groups/:id/expenses/:expenseId` | | 204 | 404 |
| `POST /groups/:id/payments` | `{from, to, amount}` | 201 the payment | 400 invalid, 404 unknown group |
| `GET /groups/:id/payments` | | 200 `{payments}`, sorted by id | 404 |
| `GET /groups/:id/balances` | | 200 `{balances}` | 404 |
| `GET /groups/:id/settle-up` | | 200 `{payments}`, suggested, not recorded | 404 |

An expense is shown as `{id, description, payer, amount, split, shares}`, where `shares` maps each name in `split` to what that person's part of the expense is. A payment is `{id, from, to, amount}`: `from` pays `to` back. Expense ids and payment ids each count up from 1 across all groups and are never reused.

**Shares.** An expense is shared equally, in whole cents, by the people in its `split`. When the amount does not divide evenly, the first people in `split` pay one cent more each, so the shares always add up to the amount: 10.00 split between Ann, Ben and Cara is 3.34, 3.33 and 3.33.

**Balances.** `balances` maps every member, in the group's member order, to what the group owes them (positive) or what they owe the group (negative). The payer of an expense is owed its amount, and each person in its `split` owes their share. A payment raises `from`'s balance and lowers `to`'s by its amount. The balances of a group always add up to 0.

**Settling up.** `GET /groups/:id/settle-up` suggests the payments `[{from, to, amount}]` that would bring every balance to 0, without recording them. While someone owes money, the member who owes the most pays the member who is owed the most the smaller of those two amounts; on a tie, the member who comes first in the group's member order goes first.

**Editing.** `PATCH` changes only the fields its body gives, each checked by the same rule as on `POST`; the others keep their value. Shares and balances always follow the expense as it is now.

**Rules**
- `id` (group): 1 to 30 characters of `a-z`, `0-9` and `-`, starting with a letter.
- `name` (group): a non-empty string of at most 100 characters.
- `members`: an array of 2 to 20 different member names. A member name is 1 to 30 characters of `A-Z`, `a-z`, `0-9`, `_` and `-`, starting with a letter; letter case matters.
- `description`: a non-empty string of at most 200 characters.
- `payer`, `from`, `to`: members of the group; `from` and `to` must differ.
- `amount`: a JSON number from 0.01 to 1000000 with at most 2 decimals, such as `12.5` or `4.35`. It is kept as whole cents and shown back as the same number.
- `split`: optional, a non-empty array of different members of the group. Without it the expense is split between every member, in the group's member order.
- Request bodies are JSON objects of at most 10 KB: a bigger body gets 413, a body that is not a JSON object gets 400. Unknown fields are ignored.
- Every error is `{"error": "<message>"}`. An unknown route is 404 `{"error": "not found"}`. Fields are checked in the order the table lists them; the first bad one decides the 400 message.

## Layout

- `server.mjs`: start-up, and the request loop: find the route, read the body, run the handler, save.
- `lib/http.mjs`: body reading, JSON replies, errors.
- `lib/routes.mjs`: route table.
- `lib/groups.mjs`, `lib/expenses.mjs`: handlers. Handlers return a new store instead of changing the old one.
- `lib/validate.mjs`: input parsers; they throw `ValidationError` (400).
- `lib/ledger.mjs`: money maths on cents: shares, balances, and how expenses and payments are shown.
- `lib/store.mjs`: loading and atomic saving of the data file.
- `test/`: `node:test` suites; `helpers.mjs` starts the app on a free port with a temp data file.
{
  "name": "split-service",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "private": true,
  "description": "A small HTTP JSON service that shares expenses within groups.",
  "type": "module",
  "engines": {
    "node": ">=24.2"
  },
  "scripts": {
    "start": "node server.mjs",
    "test": "node --test \"test/*.test.mjs\""
  }
}
// Expense and payment handlers, same contract as lib/groups.mjs: they return a new store instead of changing
// the one they get.
import { NOT_FOUND, findGroup } from './groups.mjs'
import { expenseView, paymentView } from './ledger.mjs'
import { parseAmount, parseDescription, parseMember, parseSplit, ValidationError } from './validate.mjs'

const byId = (a, b) => a.id - b.id

// The fields of a new expense in group, from a request body. Throws ValidationError on the first bad field.
export function parseExpense(group, body) {
  return {
    description: parseDescription(body.description),
    payer: parseMember(body.payer, group.members, 'payer must be a member of the group'),
    amount: parseAmount(body.amount),
    split: parseSplit(body.split, group.members),
  }
}

export function addExpense({ state, params, body }) {
  const group = findGroup(state, params[0])
  if (!group) return NOT_FOUND
  const expense = { id: state.nextExpenseId, group: group.id, ...parseExpense(group, body) }
  const next = { ...state, expenses: [...state.expenses, expense], nextExpenseId: state.nextExpenseId + 1 }
  return { status: 201, body: expenseView(expense), state: next }
}

export function listExpenses({ state, params }) {
  const group = findGroup(state, params[0])
  if (!group) return NOT_FOUND
  const expenses = state.expenses.filter(e => e.group === group.id).sort(byId).map(expenseView)
  return { status: 200, body: { expenses } }
}

const findExpense = (state, [groupId, expenseId]) =>
  state.expenses.find(e => e.group === groupId && String(e.id) === expenseId)

// Changes the fields the body gives, each checked as on POST; fields left out keep their value.
export function editExpense({ state, params, body }) {
  const group = findGroup(state, params[0])
  const old = group && findExpense(state, params)
  if (!old) return NOT_FOUND
  const changes = {}
  if ('description' in body) changes.description = parseDescription(body.description)
  if ('payer' in body) changes.payer = parseMember(body.payer, group.members, 'payer must be a member of the group')
  if ('amount' in body) changes.amount = parseAmount(body.amount)
  if ('split' in body) changes.split = parseSplit(body.split, group.members)
  const edited = { ...old, ...changes }
  const next = { ...state, expenses: state.expenses.map(e => (e === old ? edited : e)) }
  return { status: 200, body: expenseView(edited), state: next }
}

export function deleteExpense({ state, params }) {
  const expense = findExpense(state, params)
  if (!expense) return NOT_FOUND
  return { status: 204, state: { ...state, expenses: state.expenses.filter(e => e !== expense) } }
}

export function addPayment({ state, params, body }) {
  const group = findGroup(state, params[0])
  if (!group) return NOT_FOUND
  const message = 'from and to must be two different members of the group'
  const from = parseMember(body.from, group.members, message)
  const to = parseMember(body.to, group.members, message)
  if (from === to) throw new ValidationError(message)
  const payment = { id: state.nextPaymentId, group: group.id, from, to, amount: parseAmount(body.amount) }
  const next = { ...state, payments: [...state.payments, payment], nextPaymentId: state.nextPaymentId + 1 }
  return { status: 201, body: paymentView(payment), state: next }
}

export function listPayments({ state, params }) {
  const group = findGroup(state, params[0])
  if (!group) return NOT_FOUND
  const payments = state.payments.filter(p => p.group === group.id).sort(byId).map(paymentView)
  return { status: 200, body: { payments } }
}
// Group handlers. A handler gets { state, params, query, body } and returns { status, body } plus, when it
// changes the store, the new store as `state`. Handlers never change the state they are given.
import { balances, settleUp } from './ledger.mjs'
import { parseGroupId, parseGroupName, parseMembers } from './validate.mjs'

export const NOT_FOUND = { status: 404, body: { error: 'not found' } }

export const findGroup = (state, id) => state.groups.find(g => g.id === id)

export function createGroup({ state, body }) {
  const group = { id: parseGroupId(body.id), name: parseGroupName(body.name), members: parseMembers(body.members) }
  if (findGroup(state, group.id)) return { status: 409, body: { error: 'group already exists' } }
  return { status: 201, body: group, state: { ...state, groups: [...state.groups, group] } }
}

export function getGroup({ state, params }) {
  const group = findGroup(state, params[0])
  return group ? { status: 200, body: group } : NOT_FOUND
}

export function getBalances({ state, params }) {
  const group = findGroup(state, params[0])
  if (!group) return NOT_FOUND
  return { status: 200, body: { balances: balances(state, group) } }
}

export function getSettleUp({ state, params }) {
  const group = findGroup(state, params[0])
  if (!group) return NOT_FOUND
  return { status: 200, body: { payments: settleUp(state, group) } }
}
// HTTP helpers: reading a JSON body, sending JSON replies and turning errors into replies.
import { ValidationError } from './validate.mjs'

export const MAX_BODY_BYTES = 10 * 1024

export class HttpError extends Error {
  constructor(status, message) {
    super(message)
    this.status = status
  }
}

// Reads the whole body as UTF-8. Past MAX_BODY_BYTES it stops keeping chunks but still drains the upload,
// so the 413 reply reaches the client instead of a reset connection.
export function readBody(req) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const chunks = []
    let size = 0
    req.on('data', chunk => {
      size += chunk.length
      if (size <= MAX_BODY_BYTES) chunks.push(chunk)
    })
    req.on('end', () => {
      if (size > MAX_BODY_BYTES) reject(new HttpError(413, 'body too large'))
      else resolve(Buffer.concat(chunks).toString('utf8'))
    })
    req.on('error', reject)
  })
}

export function parseJsonObject(text) {
  let value
  try {
    value = JSON.parse(text)
  } catch {
    throw new HttpError(400, 'invalid JSON')
  }
  if (value === null || typeof value !== 'object' || Array.isArray(value)) {
    throw new HttpError(400, 'body must be a JSON object')
  }
  return value
}

// Sends { status, body }: body as JSON, or no body at all when it is undefined (204).
export function send(res, { status, body }) {
  if (body === undefined) {
    res.writeHead(status).end()
    return
  }
  const text = JSON.stringify(body)
  res.writeHead(status, { 'content-type': 'application/json', 'content-length': Buffer.byteLength(text) })
  res.end(text)
}

export function errorReply(err) {
  if (err instanceof HttpError) return { status: err.status, body: { error: err.message } }
  if (err instanceof ValidationError) return { status: 400, body: { error: err.message } }
  // An OS error (ENOENT, EACCES, ...) is logged as one line; any other error keeps its stack.
  console.error(err.code ? [err.code, err.syscall, err.path].filter(Boolean).join(' ') : err)
  return { status: 500, body: { error: 'internal error' } }
}
// Money maths on whole cents: how an expense is shared, what each member is owed or owes, and how to settle up.
// Amounts are stored as cents and shown by the API as numbers (435 cents is 4.35).

const CENTS_PER_UNIT = 100

export const toAmount = cents => cents / CENTS_PER_UNIT

// Each person's part of an amount in cents, as [name, cents] pairs in the order of people.
export function splitEvenly(cents, people) {
  const share = Math.floor(cents / people.length)
  return people.map(name => [name, share])
}

// An expense as the API shows it: amounts as numbers, plus each person's share keyed by name.
export function expenseView({ id, description, payer, amount, split }) {
  const shares = Object.fromEntries(splitEvenly(amount, split).map(([name, cents]) => [name, toAmount(cents)]))
  return { id, description, payer, amount: toAmount(amount), split, shares }
}

export const paymentView = ({ id, from, to, amount }) => ({ id, from, to, amount: toAmount(amount) })

// Each member's balance in cents, as a Map in the group's member order. A payer is owed the whole expense
// minus their own share; a payment from A to B moves A up and B down.
function balanceCents(state, group) {
  const cents = new Map(group.members.map(name => [name, 0]))
  const add = (name, delta) => cents.set(name, cents.get(name) + delta)
  for (const expense of state.expenses.filter(e => e.group === group.id)) {
    add(expense.payer, expense.amount)
    for (const [name, share] of splitEvenly(expense.amount, expense.split)) add(name, -share)
  }
  for (const payment of state.payments.filter(p => p.group === group.id)) {
    add(payment.from, payment.amount)
    add(payment.to, -payment.amount)
  }
  return cents
}

// What each member of the group is owed (positive) or owes (negative), in the group's member order.
export function balances(state, group) {
  return Object.fromEntries([...balanceCents(state, group)].map(([name, cents]) => [name, toAmount(cents)]))
}

// The member furthest on one side: sign 1 is owed the most, sign -1 owes the most. Ties go to the member who
// comes first in the map; null when nobody is on that side.
function furthest(cents, sign) {
  let best = null
  for (const [name, value] of cents) {
    if (value * sign > 0 && (best === null || value * sign > cents.get(best) * sign)) best = name
  }
  return best
}

// Payments that would bring every balance to 0, as [{from, to, amount}]: the member who owes the most pays the
// member who is owed the most whichever is smaller of the two, until nobody owes anything.
export function settleUp(state, group) {
  const left = balanceCents(state, group)
  const payments = []
  let from = furthest(left, -1)
  let to = furthest(left, 1)
  while (from && to) {
    const cents = Math.min(-left.get(from), left.get(to))
    payments.push({ from, to, amount: toAmount(cents) })
    left.set(from, left.get(from) + cents)
    left.set(to, left.get(to) - cents)
    from = furthest(left, -1)
    to = furthest(left, 1)
  }
  return payments
}
// Route table. `takesBody` marks the routes whose JSON body the server reads and passes on as `body`.
import { addExpense, addPayment, deleteExpense, editExpense, listExpenses, listPayments } from './expenses.mjs'
import { createGroup, getBalances, getGroup, getSettleUp } from './groups.mjs'

// Checked in order; the first match wins.
const ROUTES = [
  { method: 'POST', path: /^\/groups$/, handler: createGroup, takesBody: true },
  { method: 'GET', path: /^\/groups\/([^/]+)$/, handler: getGroup },
  { method: 'GET', path: /^\/groups\/([^/]+)\/balances$/, handler: getBalances },
  { method: 'GET', path: /^\/groups\/([^/]+)\/settle-up$/, handler: getSettleUp },
  { method: 'POST', path: /^\/groups\/([^/]+)\/expenses$/, handler: addExpense, takesBody: true },
  { method: 'GET', path: /^\/groups\/([^/]+)\/expenses$/, handler: listExpenses },
  { method: 'PATCH', path: /^\/groups\/([^/]+)\/expenses\/([^/]+)$/, handler: editExpense, takesBody: true },
  { method: 'DELETE', path: /^\/groups\/([^/]+)\/expenses\/([^/]+)$/, handler: deleteExpense },
  { method: 'POST', path: /^\/groups\/([^/]+)\/payments$/, handler: addPayment, takesBody: true },
  { method: 'GET', path: /^\/groups\/([^/]+)\/payments$/, handler: listPayments },
]

// Returns { handler, params, takesBody } for the first route matching method and pathname, or null.
export function findRoute(method, pathname) {
  for (const { method: m, path, handler, takesBody = false } of ROUTES) {
    const match = m === method && path.exec(pathname)
    if (match) return { handler, params: match.slice(1), takesBody }
  }
  return null
}
// The data file: { groups, expenses, payments, nextExpenseId, nextPaymentId } as JSON.
import { readFileSync, renameSync, rmSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs'

export const emptyStore = () => ({ groups: [], expenses: [], payments: [], nextExpenseId: 1, nextPaymentId: 1 })

const hasShape = data =>
  Array.isArray(data?.groups) &&
  Array.isArray(data.expenses) &&
  Array.isArray(data.payments) &&
  Number.isInteger(data.nextExpenseId) &&
  Number.isInteger(data.nextPaymentId)

// Reads the store from file. A missing file is an empty store; a damaged file is an error.
export function load(file) {
  let text
  try {
    text = readFileSync(file, 'utf8')
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.code === 'ENOENT') return emptyStore()
    throw err
  }
  let data
  try {
    data = JSON.parse(text)
  } catch {
    throw new Error(`data file ${file} is not valid JSON`)
  }
  if (!hasShape(data)) throw new Error(`data file ${file} has an unexpected shape`)
  return data
}

// Writes the store atomically: a temp file next to the target, then a rename over it.
export function save(file, data) {
  const tmp = `${file}.${process.pid}.tmp`
  writeFileSync(tmp, JSON.stringify(data, null, 2) + '\n')
  try {
    renameSync(tmp, file)
  } catch (err) {
    rmSync(tmp, { force: true })
    throw err
  }
}
// Input checks for request bodies and query strings. Each parser returns the clean value or throws a
// ValidationError, which the server turns into a 400 reply.

export class ValidationError extends Error {
  constructor(message) {
    super(message)
    this.name = 'ValidationError'
  }
}

const GROUP_ID = /^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,29}$/
const MEMBER_NAME = /^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,29}$/
const MIN_MEMBERS = 2
const MAX_MEMBERS = 20
const MAX_GROUP_NAME_LENGTH = 100
const MAX_DESCRIPTION_LENGTH = 200
const CENTS_PER_UNIT = 100
const MAX_AMOUNT_CENTS = 1_000_000 * CENTS_PER_UNIT
// Digits with at most two decimals, as String() writes a number: "12", "12.5", "4.35".
const TWO_DECIMALS = /^[0-9]+(\.[0-9]{1,2})?$/

const AMOUNT_MESSAGE = 'amount must be a number from 0.01 to 1000000 with at most 2 decimals'
const SPLIT_MESSAGE = 'split must be a non-empty list of different members of the group'

const isText = (v, max) => typeof v === 'string' && v.trim() !== '' && v.length <= max

export function parseGroupId(v) {
  if (typeof v !== 'string' || !GROUP_ID.test(v)) {
    throw new ValidationError('id must be 1 to 30 characters of a-z, 0-9 or -, starting with a letter')
  }
  return v
}

export function parseGroupName(v) {
  if (!isText(v, MAX_GROUP_NAME_LENGTH)) {
    throw new ValidationError(`name must be a non-empty string of at most ${MAX_GROUP_NAME_LENGTH} characters`)
  }
  return v
}

// A list of 2 to 20 member names, each used once. Names are case-sensitive: "Ann" and "ann" are two people.
export function parseMembers(v) {
  if (!Array.isArray(v) || v.length < MIN_MEMBERS || v.length > MAX_MEMBERS) {
    throw new ValidationError(`members must be an array of ${MIN_MEMBERS} to ${MAX_MEMBERS} names`)
  }
  if (!v.every(name => typeof name === 'string' && MEMBER_NAME.test(name))) {
    throw new ValidationError('member names must be 1 to 30 characters of A-Z, a-z, 0-9, _ or -, starting with a letter')
  }
  if (new Set(v).size !== v.length) throw new ValidationError('members must not repeat a name')
  return [...v]
}

export function parseDescription(v) {
  if (!isText(v, MAX_DESCRIPTION_LENGTH)) {
    throw new ValidationError(`description must be a non-empty string of at most ${MAX_DESCRIPTION_LENGTH} characters`)
  }
  return v
}

// Amounts arrive as numbers such as 12.5 or 4.35 and are kept as whole cents, so sums never drift.
export function parseAmount(v) {
  if (typeof v !== 'number' || !TWO_DECIMALS.test(String(v))) throw new ValidationError(AMOUNT_MESSAGE)
  const cents = Math.trunc(v * CENTS_PER_UNIT)
  if (cents < 1 || cents > MAX_AMOUNT_CENTS) throw new ValidationError(AMOUNT_MESSAGE)
  return cents
}

// A name that must belong to one of members; message says which field was wrong.
export function parseMember(v, members, message) {
  if (typeof v !== 'string' || !members.includes(v)) throw new ValidationError(message)
  return v
}

// Who shares an expense: a non-empty list of members without repeats. Missing means every member, in group order.
export function parseSplit(v, members) {
  if (v === undefined) return [...members]
  if (!Array.isArray(v) || v.length === 0 || new Set(v).size !== v.length) throw new ValidationError(SPLIT_MESSAGE)
  if (!v.every(name => typeof name === 'string' && members.includes(name))) throw new ValidationError(SPLIT_MESSAGE)
  return [...v]
}
