+   - `bad-type`: `type` is not `"expense"` or `"payment"`.
+   - `unknown-field`: a field its type does not take. An expense takes `type`, `description`, `payer`, `amount` and `split`; a payment takes `type`, `from`, `to` and `amount`.
+   - Expense: `bad-description`, `bad-payer`, `bad-amount`, `bad-split`; then `duplicate` when an earlier entry that broke none of the rules above is an expense with the same payer, amount and description; then `already-recorded` when the group already has an expense with the same payer, amount and description. Descriptions are compared after `trim()` and `toLowerCase()`, amounts in cents; `split` is not compared. An earlier entry counts for `duplicate` even when it is itself `duplicate` or `already-recorded`, skipped or not.
+   - Payment: `bad-from` (`from` is not a member), `bad-to` (`to` is not a member, or is `from`), `bad-amount`. Payments are never `duplicate` or `already-recorded`.
